_refs":["bnd-d198444334a75731"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"The coverage mapping boundary performs an exact need-text lookup against supplied capabilities, retains allowed record identifiers, and correctly marks missing capability matches as unsupported. It does not create independent market-demand claims.","evidence_refs":["bnd-d198444334a75731"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":"trusted_for_reuse","unit_id":"bnd-d198444334a75731"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"verdict":"met"}],"decision":"trusted","decision_reason":"The prioritization boundary ranks unsupported needs before covered needs, then uses upstream provenance rank within each group. That explains the observed priority order and does not itself add unsupported demand evidence.","evidence_refs":["bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":"trusted_for_reuse","unit_id":"bnd-42028d4dc2fb42fe"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"verdict":"not_met"}],"decision":"failed","decision_reason":"Root cause. The upstream demand selection treats every supplied corpus row with demand_score >= 3, plus fallback rows, as demand-bearing. The supplied package contains need labels and scores but no observed jobs, pain, triggers, alternatives, consequences, or outcomes supporting customer demand. Under the strict market-demand criteria, this selected unsupported and generic pipeline-maintenance candidates as market demand, including the top recommended need.","evidence_refs":["bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":null,"unit_id":"bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"],"verdict":"not_met"}],"decision":"suspect","decision_reason":"This boundary normalizes and retains the selected records but does not add or verify the missing market-demand evidence. It propagates unsupported demand records, including the record that becomes the final top recommendation. The defect appears introduced upstream in demand selection, so this is propagation rather than the top root cause.","evidence_refs":["bnd-82e7965b4741e42f","bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":null,"unit_id":"bnd-82e7965b4741e42f"},{"boundary_health_acknowledged":true,"criteria_outcomes":[{"criterion":"preserve the two exact handoffs","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5"],"verdict":"met"},{"criterion":"produce the required deterministic recommendation","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5"],"verdict":"not_met"}],"decision":"suspect","decision_reason":"This boundary ranks normalized need records by demand_score and assembles the evidence-source handoff. Because the normalized needs lack direct market-demand support, the provenance ranking gives unsupported demand labels unwarranted priority. The first fault remains demand selection, but this boundary materially propagates that unsupported ranking into the downstream job.","evidence_refs":["bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5","bnd-fec3a1acc50a0ab3"],"expand_helper_prefixes":[],"inspect_artifacts":[],"suspect_node_refs":[],"trust_level":null,"unit_id":"bnd-3beaadce814c2ac5"}]},"review_sha256":"